Found while fixing k313. In ticket mode, karr-foundation --dry-run --verbose logs "STALL task#5 -- no report from the agent" for the agent run it did not start. Nothing is written (no .karr.state, no block), so it is cosmetic, but a dry run should not report a stall for a run that never happened.

Repro (ex/setup.sh copied into scratchpad, config.yml from setup): karr-foundation --dry-run --verbose printed 'STALL task#5 -- no report from the agent' right after 'DRY-RUN (skipped)' for webapp (mode: ticket). docs-site (mode: drain) printed no STALL: a drain judges engagement and a run that never started engages nothing, so drain mode was not affected. Cause: Runner returns (0, '') for a dry run and _drain_repo judged that like a real run; in ticket mode the unmoved card became outcome stall + STALL line. Fix: 'last if $self->dry_run;' in _drain_repo right after _run_command, before any judging -- outcome idle, TICKET/START/DRY-RUN lines stay. Regression in t/185 (ticket dry run: no STALL, outcome not stall, no .karr.log/.karr.state, card unblocked) failed 2 assertions before the fix; drain-mode companion subtest passes before and after (pins one would-be START, no loop). No POD states what a dry run logs, so no POD change.

